  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 1502.01 Certification Required",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 1502.01 Certification Required.\n\n(a) Except as specified by (b) below, no person shall distribute or use a waste-derived product within New Hampshire unless the product is:\n\n(1) Certified for distribution and use in accordance with this chapter; and\n\n(2) Used in accordance with the provisions of the certification.\n\n(b) A person distributing and using wood ash for agricultural land application shall comply with the requirements of Env-Sw 1700 instead of the requirements of (a) above.\n\nSource. #6619-B, eff 10-29-97; (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Sw 1500); ss by #8459, eff 10-28-05 (formerly Env-Wm 3202.01); ss by #10599, eff 7-1-14; ss by #14067, eff 9-3-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-sw1500.html"
